# Link's proof of a parameter is tested for in front of a copy only where one look at the value settles it: primitives, one layout, or both.
# A family or a set of closures grows with the program, and so would each question about it and each test of it, at every copy: members times copies.
# Here the parameter is one of two layouts. The copy asks for them where it reads, as a guess with the call as written beside it.
# RUN: walk f2 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f2:Body
# CHECK: frame 1 callee=f1
# CHECK: isInLoop=true isLoopHead=true
# CHECK: [[element]]: anything{{*}} = Call
# CHECK-NOT: = TypeTest [[element]]
# CHECK: = CallDirect [[element]] function=f1 [isNeverInlined]
